# __GAME__

A co-op game on [unified](https://github.com/FylmTM/godot-unified) (deterministic rollback netcode, Odin + Godot), started
from `uni init`: each player moves a dot. Make it yours from here.

```
./uni run              # play (uni.cmd on Windows)
./uni test --suite all # the sim tests and the game under headless Godot
./uni headless -- synctest --ticks 600 --window 8 # the sim without Godot (-- help: every mode)
./uni help             # every command
```

- `simulation/__GAME__/`: the deterministic sim (unified/src/sim/SPEC.md: f32 only, no pointers in the state).
- `simulation/headless/`: the headless binary (offline runs, sync-tests, benchmarks).
- `simulation/extension/`: the GDExtension: the sim run by unified's Godot host, and how the state becomes views.
- `simulation/tests/`: the sim's tests and the determinism lint.
- `game/`: the Godot side: scenes, views and scripts. GDScript reads the sim; input is the only way in.
- `tools/`: this game's CLI (unified's public commands, plus the game's own).
- `unified/`: unified, as a git submodule. Local paths (a Godot install, the EOS SDK) go in a git-ignored `.env`.
